1
00:00:01,251 --> 00:00:03,086
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor… ♪

2
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:09,009
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:09,092 --> 00:00:10,635
♪ Oh, Mister Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,719 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,307
♪ One cut, and it’s over ♪

6
00:00:16,850 --> 00:00:19,185
Who is this woman with Atoy?

7
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,270
I don't know her.

8
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:23,189
Rommel: Bro, don't get mad, okay?

9
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:26,735
I used your picture
when I was chatting with Chanty.

10
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:27,360
Huh?!

11
00:00:27,444 --> 00:00:29,779
Gavin: Bro,
you need to tell Chanty the truth.

12
00:00:29,863 --> 00:00:31,781
If you like her, do it right.

13
00:00:31,865 --> 00:00:34,367
Who is this woman and
why are you hugging each other?!

14
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:36,327
Atoy: Her name is Georgia.

15
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:37,787
Women: Georgia?!

16
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,205
Atoy: She-- she-- she tripped.

17
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:41,249
And then I just helped her.

18
00:00:41,332 --> 00:00:42,292
- And then suddenly there was a-
- Audrey: What about this?!

19
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:43,084
Huh?

20
00:00:43,168 --> 00:00:45,295
Maybe this is Jesabel's.

21
00:00:45,378 --> 00:00:46,963
Women: Jesabel?!

22
00:00:47,046 --> 00:00:50,842
Ah, would you know where Atoy lives?

23
00:00:50,925 --> 00:00:52,719
[music continues]

24
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,471
Emerson: Could it be
that you took the picture?

25
00:00:55,055 --> 00:00:56,514
You gave it to Audrey?

26
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:57,348
Huh?!

27
00:00:57,432 --> 00:00:59,100
Maybe the picture just fell.

28
00:00:59,184 --> 00:01:00,727
You're the one who told the dance club

29
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,187
that she's adopted, right?

30
00:01:02,270 --> 00:01:03,271
No, I didn't!

31
00:01:03,813 --> 00:01:04,814
Ouch!

32
00:01:04,898 --> 00:01:06,399
Why did you push Hailey?!

33
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:11,780
There's a private
wedding at the beach resort.

34
00:01:11,863 --> 00:01:14,032
Rasta Dub Crew, they're gonna perform

35
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:15,325
at the wedding reception.

36
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:18,620
Belladonna: So, if you guys
can find a way to perform with them,

37
00:01:18,703 --> 00:01:20,288
I think that will be your way in.

38
00:01:20,371 --> 00:01:22,874
Where is Tatoy?

39
00:01:22,957 --> 00:01:24,250
Audrey: He left early, my child.

40
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:26,211
He went to see a client.

41
00:01:26,294 --> 00:01:26,920
Wait, wait, wait.

42
00:01:27,003 --> 00:01:28,338
Did you tell your wife where you're going?

43
00:01:28,421 --> 00:01:29,756
[music continues]

44
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:31,925
I have eyes on Atoy Padua.

45
00:01:32,008 --> 00:01:34,177
Don't take your eyes off Atoy.

46
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,470
Elias: Do we understand each other?

47
00:01:35,553 --> 00:01:39,057
Remember, okay, you're just
support for the band's percussion.

48
00:01:39,140 --> 00:01:41,184
I know someone at Indigo Pearl

49
00:01:41,267 --> 00:01:42,227
who will help you.

50
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,436
Ah, thank you, Sir.

51
00:01:44,813 --> 00:01:46,856
[music continues]

52
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,399
Apologies. Here.

53
00:02:32,569 --> 00:02:33,194
Oscar: Audrey.

54
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:35,071
Here's some bread.

55
00:02:35,155 --> 00:02:36,364
You probably haven’t eaten yet.

56
00:02:36,447 --> 00:02:38,032
You're so sweet. Thank you.

57
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:40,368
By the way, where is…

58
00:02:40,451 --> 00:02:41,786
Atoy? He wasn't here this morning.

59
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:44,122
When I left,
it seems he left a bit too early.

60
00:02:44,956 --> 00:02:47,417
As usual, a client.

61
00:02:48,126 --> 00:02:50,753
But look, he sent a picture.

62
00:02:51,462 --> 00:02:52,714
There, look.

63
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:55,341
[phone ringing]

64
00:02:55,425 --> 00:02:56,843
Ms. Dolly is calling.

65
00:02:56,926 --> 00:02:57,886
[phone blips]

66
00:02:57,969 --> 00:02:59,888
Ah, hello, Ma'am, Ms. Dolly.

67
00:02:59,971 --> 00:03:00,722
Dolly on the phone: Hi, Audrey!

68
00:03:00,805 --> 00:03:02,640
I left my laptop in my office.

69
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:05,101
Can you please bring it to me now?

70
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:07,228
I'm at the Indigo Pearl resort right now.

71
00:03:07,312 --> 00:03:09,981
I'll send you the address. It's a bit far.

72
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:11,316
Just have Oka take you.

73
00:03:11,399 --> 00:03:12,650
Um, yes.

74
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:14,903
On the way.

75
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:15,820
Let's go?

76
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:16,905
Let's go.

77
00:03:16,988 --> 00:03:18,114
[rousing music playing]

78
00:03:18,197 --> 00:03:19,657
Your bread.

79
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,617
It's a long trip going there.

80
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,327
[theme music playing]

81
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:24,704
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

82
00:03:24,787 --> 00:03:30,126
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

83
00:03:30,877 --> 00:03:32,545
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

84
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:34,297
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

85
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,924
♪ The hole in my polo

86
00:03:36,007 --> 00:03:38,009
that's right under the armpit ♪

87
00:03:38,092 --> 00:03:40,220
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

88
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:41,971
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

89
00:03:42,055 --> 00:03:44,015
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

90
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:48,895
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

91
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:49,687
[gunshots]

92
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:51,105
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

93
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,524
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

94
00:03:53,608 --> 00:03:54,943
[music swells]

95
00:03:56,736 --> 00:03:58,112
[music fades]

96
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:01,783
[muffled chattering]

97
00:04:01,866 --> 00:04:05,245
Wanbol, during recess

98
00:04:05,328 --> 00:04:06,746
you're wide awake.

99
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:09,874
But during class you're sleepy.

100
00:04:10,458 --> 00:04:13,711
Why are you always sleepy?

101
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:17,006
Didn't I tell you, I study at night?

102
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,010
Well, it's because, Wanbol, ah…

103
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,888
I saw something.

104
00:04:23,972 --> 00:04:26,766
I saw you on TV.

105
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:31,145
You were pulling a box of fish.

106
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:35,358
Are you a vendor or
a porter at the market?

107
00:04:35,858 --> 00:04:38,069
Is that the reason…

108
00:04:38,152 --> 00:04:41,155
you always smell like
fish and are always sleepy?

109
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:43,116
No, that wasn't me.

110
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:45,076
Wanbol, don't worry, it's just me.

111
00:04:45,159 --> 00:04:46,160
It's just me.

112
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:49,622
You can tell me anything.

113
00:04:51,374 --> 00:04:54,961
There's nothing wrong
with being a vendor or a porter.

114
00:04:55,628 --> 00:05:01,050
You know, I used to live on the street.

115
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:04,220
Mmm-hmm. And then
I sold native rice delicacies.

116
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:06,055
Mmm, that was delicious, you know.

117
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:08,099
But I wasn't ashamed!

118
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:09,309
I really wasn't ashamed.

119
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:10,310
Really!

120
00:05:10,393 --> 00:05:12,186
Fine.

121
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:15,064
I do odd jobs at the market

122
00:05:15,148 --> 00:05:17,150
so I'd have money for meals and fare.

123
00:05:19,068 --> 00:05:21,654
I hope we're still
friends even if I'm just like this.

124
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,323
What do you mean by that?

125
00:05:23,406 --> 00:05:25,408
I admire you, you know! Mmm-mmm.

126
00:05:25,992 --> 00:05:28,745
You're not only kind,
you're hardworking too!

127
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:30,621
Oh, high five, high five. Mmm.

128
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:35,293
And we're friends forever.

129
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:37,170
No matter what you are! Yes.

130
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:41,257
Just, take a bath every day, okay?

131
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:43,092
We're good.

132
00:05:43,968 --> 00:05:45,344
Ibyang: We're Team…

133
00:05:46,304 --> 00:05:47,889
Team…

134
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:49,390
Byang-Bol!

135
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:51,893
Byang-Bol, yes.

136
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:54,270
Ibyang and Wanbol.

137
00:05:54,353 --> 00:05:56,147
Byang-Bol for the win!

138
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,482
Wah, ah! [claps]

139
00:05:57,982 --> 00:05:59,400
Don't forget!

140
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:00,985
Take a bath every day, okay?

141
00:06:01,069 --> 00:06:02,195
Yes, I promise you that.

142
00:06:02,278 --> 00:06:04,238
I'll always take a bath every day.

143
00:06:04,322 --> 00:06:05,656
Oh, okay. Oh, high five again.

144
00:06:05,740 --> 00:06:06,365
Wah. [claps]

145
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:10,119
[light music playing]

146
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:11,913
Oka, Oka!

147
00:06:11,996 --> 00:06:14,624
I talked to Ms. Dolly,
she's not in her room,

148
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:16,584
she's at the wedding reception.

149
00:06:16,667 --> 00:06:17,710
Let's go find her.

150
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:18,503
Okay.

151
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,588
But where could that be?

152
00:06:22,048 --> 00:06:22,840
I don't know either.

153
00:06:22,924 --> 00:06:23,925
This is all I saw.

154
00:06:24,008 --> 00:06:24,592
- It's so beautiful, look.
- Miss, miss,

155
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:27,261
ah, do you know where
the wedding reception is?

156
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:28,471
Ah, miss, just walk over there.

157
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,223
You'll see the signages.

158
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:31,641
Ah, okay. Thank you.

159
00:06:33,351 --> 00:06:34,060
Let's go.

160
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:36,062
It's so beautiful.

161
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:37,605
I'll bring Atoy here one day.

162
00:06:38,856 --> 00:06:40,733
Mmm. Let's go!

163
00:06:40,817 --> 00:06:42,151
Oh, let's go. She said it's there.

164
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:44,362
Let's go.

165
00:06:45,613 --> 00:06:47,865
[rousing music playing]

166
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:49,283
- Hi!
- Yeah!

167
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,286
Guys, we have a problem, Audrey is here.

168
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:53,162
- Oh.
- Huh?

169
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:54,747
What is she doing here?

170
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:55,998
Did she follow you here?

171
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:57,208
I don't know either.

172
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:58,793
She's with Oka.

173
00:06:58,876 --> 00:07:00,920
Oka?! Again?!

174
00:07:01,003 --> 00:07:01,671
Hey. What’s the matter with you?

175
00:07:01,754 --> 00:07:04,006
That Oka is really annoying.

176
00:07:04,090 --> 00:07:05,591
Psst, buddy, come on.

177
00:07:05,675 --> 00:07:07,635
Relax, focus, focus.

178
00:07:08,136 --> 00:07:10,138
I knew they were coming to this reception,

179
00:07:10,221 --> 00:07:11,055
they're probably meeting someone.

180
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:14,058
But, we should just focus on our mission.

181
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,768
Washer, that's who we need to find,

182
00:07:15,852 --> 00:07:16,352
The Washer.

183
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,896
After that, we can go home.

184
00:07:19,772 --> 00:07:20,481
Oh, here.

185
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:21,899
Here, I'll give you these.

186
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:23,860
While we're playing, scan

187
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:25,111
the whole surroundings,

188
00:07:25,194 --> 00:07:26,904
so that whoever is suspicious,

189
00:07:26,988 --> 00:07:28,072
we can play it back.

190
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:30,408
That also has a bluetooth device

191
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:31,993
- so we can hear each other.
- Oh, oh--I like that.

192
00:07:32,076 --> 00:07:33,536
This is mine. This, this is mine.

193
00:07:33,619 --> 00:07:34,537
Mmm-- where's mine?

194
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:35,413
This is mine!

195
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:37,415
Why are you even fighting over it?

196
00:07:37,498 --> 00:07:39,375
Jesabel: Why? Are
you a tracker in training?

197
00:07:39,459 --> 00:07:40,918
Okay. Then fine, it's yours.

198
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:41,919
- It's yours.
- Testing, testing.

199
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:42,712
I don't need that anyway.

200
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:43,880
I have bionic eyes, you know.

201
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:44,505
Oh, there's bluetooth--

202
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:46,215
That would only ruin my OOTD.

203
00:07:46,299 --> 00:07:48,134
Guys, let's go! We're about to start!

204
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:49,802
Come on, let's go.

205
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:50,803
Let's go.

206
00:07:50,887 --> 00:07:52,346
Okay, ah. Okay.

207
00:07:52,430 --> 00:07:53,055
[upbeat reggae music playing]

208
00:07:53,139 --> 00:07:54,265
Emerson: Rastafari!

209
00:07:54,348 --> 00:07:55,224
[music fades]

210
00:07:55,308 --> 00:07:56,934
There. Look,
there are even light displays.

211
00:07:57,518 --> 00:07:58,895
It's so beautiful!

212
00:07:58,978 --> 00:07:59,562
Oh.

213
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:01,439
Wow.

214
00:08:01,522 --> 00:08:02,023
[camera shutter snaps]

215
00:08:02,106 --> 00:08:03,941
Audrey, did you bring my laptop?

216
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:05,193
- Ms. Dolly!
- Of course, you did.

217
00:08:05,276 --> 00:08:06,235
Yes!

218
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,528
- Thank you so much.
- Here you go.

219
00:08:08,070 --> 00:08:09,405
I love your shoes!

220
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:10,907
Thank you!

221
00:08:10,990 --> 00:08:12,241
The color is so cute.

222
00:08:12,325 --> 00:08:13,951
You know, my niece, the bridesmaid,

223
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:15,620
just lent those to me.

224
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:18,080
Wait. Ah, why don't you guys

225
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:19,707
have some food first?

226
00:08:19,790 --> 00:08:21,417
There's an outdoor resto,

227
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,127
go there, order whatever.

228
00:08:23,211 --> 00:08:24,462
Don't worry, tab is on me.

229
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:25,630
Ah, no need, Miss.

230
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:26,672
It's not necessary.

231
00:08:27,423 --> 00:08:29,342
Don't tell me you're
going home right away?

232
00:08:29,425 --> 00:08:30,718
It took so long to get here,

233
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:33,679
and I'm so sure
there's traffic going home.

234
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:35,932
Dolly: Come on, guys!

235
00:08:36,015 --> 00:08:37,391
What a waste of this beautiful place,

236
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:38,601
if we leave right away.

237
00:08:38,684 --> 00:08:39,352
Dolly: Yes!

238
00:08:40,102 --> 00:08:41,979
Go on. Audrey, go on.

239
00:08:42,063 --> 00:08:43,356
All you need to do is walk past

240
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:44,732
the wedding reception area,

241
00:08:44,815 --> 00:08:46,859
that's where the outdoor resto is.

242
00:08:46,943 --> 00:08:48,444
And then, I'll meet you guys there

243
00:08:48,528 --> 00:08:49,529
in a little bit.

244
00:08:49,612 --> 00:08:50,196
Yes?

245
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,073
Say yes.

246
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:54,033
Yes is the only answer. Bye, bye!

247
00:08:54,116 --> 00:08:54,825
See you!

248
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:56,410
[rousing music playing]

249
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:57,245
Say yes.

250
00:08:58,788 --> 00:08:59,914
Right? Nice, right?

251
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:00,665
Let's go!

252
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,208
Okay, fine.

253
00:09:04,877 --> 00:09:07,213
[lively chatter]

254
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:22,645
[muffled chattering]

255
00:09:24,063 --> 00:09:27,149
[music continues]

256
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:40,830
[device blips]

257
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:44,000
Any ah, suspicious prospects?

258
00:09:44,083 --> 00:09:45,751
[muffled chattering]

259
00:09:45,835 --> 00:09:46,961
I have so many prospects,

260
00:09:47,044 --> 00:09:49,213
but none are suspicious.

261
00:09:49,922 --> 00:09:52,842
But I have a prospect, and it's delicious.

262
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,468
[muffled chattering]

263
00:09:54,552 --> 00:09:58,514
[music continues]

264
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:05,980
[device blips]

265
00:10:06,063 --> 00:10:07,023
Guys, guys,

266
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:08,858
Audrey is at 10 o'clock.

267
00:10:08,941 --> 00:10:11,444
[muffled chattering]

268
00:10:11,527 --> 00:10:15,573
[tense music playing]

269
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:35,801
'Toy, 2 o'clock.

270
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,637
2 o'clock, 'Toy! 2 o'clock.

271
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:38,721
[muffled chattering]

272
00:10:38,804 --> 00:10:40,139
[music continues]

273
00:10:40,222 --> 00:10:40,765
Uh-o.

274
00:10:41,682 --> 00:10:43,893
Oh no, those two should never meet.

275
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:46,979
[device blips]

276
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:51,067
[muffled chattering]

277
00:10:51,734 --> 00:10:54,570
[music continues]

278
00:11:00,451 --> 00:11:00,951
[phone blips]

279
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:04,121
[muffled chattering in the distance]

280
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:06,207
Bro, Chanty is
apparently at the tailoring shop.

281
00:11:08,167 --> 00:11:10,294
Karla and I are meeting there too.

282
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:12,338
Bro, we can't meet each other, okay?

283
00:11:12,421 --> 00:11:13,297
This is what we’ll do.

284
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:15,424
I'll just go to Chanty first.

285
00:11:15,508 --> 00:11:16,550
Then I'll tell her

286
00:11:16,634 --> 00:11:18,677
that you'll meet her at the coffee shop,

287
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,262
so she'll leave the area.

288
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:20,930
And then from there,

289
00:11:21,013 --> 00:11:22,848
you just follow to meet
Karla at the tailoring shop.

290
00:11:22,932 --> 00:11:23,641
Okay?

291
00:11:23,724 --> 00:11:24,475
[scoffs]

292
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:25,810
Bro, I won't meet
Chanty at the coffee shop.

293
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:26,685
Bro, come on.

294
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:28,396
It'll just take a moment, just 5 minutes.

295
00:11:28,479 --> 00:11:29,563
Just small talk.

296
00:11:29,647 --> 00:11:31,690
Come on, dude. It's me.

297
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:33,692
Come on.

298
00:11:34,193 --> 00:11:34,860
Fine, alright.

299
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:37,696
As long as you take
care of my economics, okay?

300
00:11:38,614 --> 00:11:39,323
Finish that, okay?

301
00:11:39,407 --> 00:11:40,074
I got you, bro.

302
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:42,326
Sorry for the hassle, okay?

303
00:11:42,410 --> 00:11:45,037
[zipping]

304
00:11:45,121 --> 00:11:46,163
Okay, bro. I'll go ahead!

305
00:11:48,082 --> 00:11:49,375
[muffled chattering in the distance]

306
00:11:49,458 --> 00:11:50,292
[lively chatter]

307
00:11:50,376 --> 00:11:52,420
Oh, oh-- I'm sorry!

308
00:11:52,503 --> 00:11:53,045
[gasps]

309
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:55,673
[muffled chattering]

310
00:11:55,756 --> 00:11:59,343
[suspicious music playing]

311
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:01,595
It's okay.

312
00:12:03,806 --> 00:12:04,432
[music fades]

313
00:12:05,099 --> 00:12:06,642
They almost collided there, you know.

314
00:12:07,393 --> 00:12:09,603
After the set, let's split up first, okay?

315
00:12:09,687 --> 00:12:10,855
Let's focus on the Washer.

316
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:13,065
And then afterwards,
once we have information,

317
00:12:13,649 --> 00:12:14,316
we'll leave.

318
00:12:16,026 --> 00:12:16,986
Copy, copy, copy.

319
00:12:18,446 --> 00:12:19,488
Copy, sir.

320
00:12:19,572 --> 00:12:22,450
[muffled chattering]

321
00:12:42,928 --> 00:12:44,263
[music fades]

322
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:47,266
[sneaky music playing]

323
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:48,809
Karla: Chanty?

324
00:12:49,351 --> 00:12:50,686
What are you doing here?

325
00:12:52,563 --> 00:12:54,064
Do we know each other?

326
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,733
Ah, I'm Karla.

327
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:57,568
We met at your fan meet and greet,

328
00:12:57,651 --> 00:12:58,777
I was with Denden.

329
00:12:58,861 --> 00:13:00,362
She's the super fan.

330
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:02,406
Oh, wait. Let me
message her that you're here.

331
00:13:02,490 --> 00:13:03,782
Oh, can you not for now?

332
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:06,410
Ah, I'm meeting someone today.

333
00:13:06,994 --> 00:13:08,078
Who?

334
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:09,246
[chuckles softly]

335
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,874
Ah, I'm meeting
the person I'm chatting with.

336
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,542
You're chatting with someone?

337
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:14,335
Mmm-hmm.

338
00:13:14,418 --> 00:13:15,419
Here in Baclaran?

339
00:13:16,253 --> 00:13:16,795
Yes.

340
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,297
Ahh.

341
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:20,424
It might be a scammer, okay, be careful.

342
00:13:20,925 --> 00:13:21,967
Oh, no.

343
00:13:22,051 --> 00:13:24,386
I've already met him and
he's super handsome, you know.

344
00:13:25,387 --> 00:13:27,473
There are handsome scammers too.

345
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:29,350
Ah, anyway!

346
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:30,851
I have something I need to do.

347
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,394
- I'll go ahead.
- All right.

348
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:35,231
[music continues]

349
00:13:35,314 --> 00:13:36,774
[sighs, then clicks tongue]

350
00:13:37,650 --> 00:13:38,984
Where could he be?

351
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:41,820
Should I chat him up?

352
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:44,114
Chanty, hi.

353
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:46,951
Hi!

354
00:13:47,034 --> 00:13:48,619
[suspicious music playing]

355
00:13:48,702 --> 00:13:49,745
Do I know you?

356
00:13:50,538 --> 00:13:52,665
Ah, I'm Rommel.

357
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,209
I'm Gavin’s friend.

358
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:57,670
By the way, he asked me to fetch you.

359
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:58,837
He says to meet at the coffee shop.

360
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:01,382
Oh, really?

361
00:14:01,465 --> 00:14:03,467
Okay. Where is he?

362
00:14:03,551 --> 00:14:05,719
[music fades]

363
00:14:05,803 --> 00:14:09,723
[ominous music playing]

364
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:19,441
[thuds]

365
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,442
Oscar: Ow!

366
00:14:20,526 --> 00:14:21,485
[groans]

367
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:23,863
[tense music playing]

368
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:24,446
Atoy.

369
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:27,283
[music swells]

370
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:29,034
I knew I recognized you!

371
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:30,494
Oscar: What are you doing here?

372
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:33,831
[suspicious music playing]

373
00:14:33,914 --> 00:14:34,415
Buddy.

374
00:14:34,915 --> 00:14:35,666
[Oscar grunts]

375
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:38,085
- What are you doing here?
- It hurts.

376
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:40,462
[music continues]

377
00:14:40,546 --> 00:14:41,755
Well, I accompanied Audrey.

378
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,091
Our boss asked us to do something.

379
00:14:44,174 --> 00:14:46,802
You? What are you doing here? Why--

380
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:49,930
Do you have a secret mission again?

381
00:14:50,014 --> 00:14:50,890
Something like that.

382
00:14:51,974 --> 00:14:53,392
Buddy, can you…

383
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:55,185
Buddy, don't tell Audrey.

384
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,605
Mmm. I've got you, 'Toy.

385
00:14:57,688 --> 00:14:59,273
Ah, it's better…

386
00:14:59,356 --> 00:15:01,775
Buddy, maybe it's
better if you and Audrey leave,

387
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:04,361
because Georgia is here too.

388
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:06,030
Georgia?

389
00:15:06,113 --> 00:15:07,740
The woman you were hugging in the picture?

390
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:09,783
[music continues]

391
00:15:10,826 --> 00:15:11,327
Yes.

392
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:12,995
[scoffs]

393
00:15:13,078 --> 00:15:14,788
I don't know why she's here.

394
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,707
But it's going to be tough if those two

395
00:15:16,790 --> 00:15:17,791
meet each other.

396
00:15:21,211 --> 00:15:25,633
[suspicious music playing]

397
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,275
[music swells]

398
00:15:44,026 --> 00:15:45,694
Her name is Georgia.

399
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:47,321
Women: Georgia?!

400
00:15:47,404 --> 00:15:48,656
[music fades]

401
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:51,116
Excuse me.

402
00:15:51,825 --> 00:15:53,619
Audrey: Are you Georgia?

403
00:15:55,579 --> 00:15:56,413
Yes.

404
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:58,874
Have we met?

405
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:00,960
I'm Audrey Padua,

406
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:03,420
wife of Anthony Padua.

407
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:06,423
Oh, Atoy's wife is so beautiful.

408
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:09,218
How come you know me?

409
00:16:09,301 --> 00:16:10,761
Did he tell you about me?

410
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:12,638
No.

411
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:15,391
There's a picture of you and my husband

412
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:17,351
hugging outside a cafe,

413
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:21,188
so I'm trying to find out who you are.

414
00:16:21,271 --> 00:16:23,315
Oh, okay.

415
00:16:24,525 --> 00:16:27,444
Ah, I'm sure it was
a wrongly timed snapshot.

416
00:16:28,612 --> 00:16:29,530
It should be,

417
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:31,865
because if not…

418
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:35,327
we wouldn't be having a conversation.

419
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:37,579
What brings you here?

420
00:16:37,663 --> 00:16:39,373
Are you with Atoy?

421
00:16:39,456 --> 00:16:41,750
No. Ah, I'm here for my boss.

422
00:16:42,626 --> 00:16:44,253
She's a guest at the wedding.

423
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:45,838
You?

424
00:16:46,964 --> 00:16:48,132
Why are you here?

425
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:49,633
Who are you with?

426
00:16:49,717 --> 00:16:50,759
I'm alone.

427
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:54,304
You-- you know, solo staycation.

428
00:16:54,388 --> 00:16:56,473
I actually passed by
the wedding reception earlier.

429
00:16:56,557 --> 00:16:57,766
Georgia: It was so fun,

430
00:16:57,850 --> 00:16:59,101
because there was a reggae band.

431
00:16:59,184 --> 00:17:00,728
So, I joined in.

432
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:03,230
Joined in?

433
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,942
Do you mean you gatecrashed?

434
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:08,569
I guess so. I guess
it's better to gatecrash

435
00:17:08,652 --> 00:17:09,987
a wedding party than to disturb

436
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,947
someone else's marriage, right?

437
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:15,075
[rousing music playing]

438
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:18,287
Here you go.

439
00:17:18,829 --> 00:17:19,788
Thank you.

440
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:22,082
Ah, Chanty, are you okay?

441
00:17:24,043 --> 00:17:26,253
I'm just really excited.

442
00:17:26,336 --> 00:17:28,464
After months of chatting,

443
00:17:29,506 --> 00:17:31,925
this is sort of like
our first date, you know?

444
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,928
Will he like me?

445
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:36,638
[chuckles]

446
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:37,514
Of course.

447
00:17:38,098 --> 00:17:39,391
Your chats wouldn't have lasted

448
00:17:39,475 --> 00:17:40,517
if not, right?

449
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:41,810
Rommel: And…

450
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:43,520
[clears throat]

451
00:17:43,604 --> 00:17:45,355
You're his dream girl.

452
00:17:46,815 --> 00:17:48,734
Hmm, okay.

453
00:17:48,817 --> 00:17:51,945
[pensive music playing]

454
00:17:54,907 --> 00:17:57,242
[playful music playing]

455
00:17:57,326 --> 00:17:57,868
It's so delicious.

456
00:17:59,078 --> 00:18:00,245
Ah, you have--

457
00:18:01,205 --> 00:18:01,789
Hmm?

458
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:03,373
- You have whipped cream on your lip.
- Huh?

459
00:18:03,457 --> 00:18:04,249
This?

460
00:18:04,333 --> 00:18:05,042
Rommel: That, that, that.

461
00:18:05,125 --> 00:18:06,085
There's nothing.

462
00:18:06,668 --> 00:18:07,377
Chanty: Huh?

463
00:18:08,587 --> 00:18:09,338
There is.

464
00:18:09,421 --> 00:18:10,172
Huh?

465
00:18:10,839 --> 00:18:11,673
Is it okay now?

466
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:15,302
[music fades]

467
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:16,428
Oh, here he comes!

468
00:18:17,346 --> 00:18:17,888
Rommel: Oh?

469
00:18:18,472 --> 00:18:19,848
[pensive music playing]

470
00:18:19,932 --> 00:18:20,849
Ah…

471
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,142
[Rommel clears throat] Chanty,

472
00:18:22,768 --> 00:18:26,105
I'm sorry for being in
a hurry to leave last time, okay.

473
00:18:26,188 --> 00:18:28,190
But I think it's best that…

474
00:18:28,857 --> 00:18:29,858
we don't meet anymore.

475
00:18:30,442 --> 00:18:32,486
Um, what he means is,

476
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:35,239
don't meet in a place like this anymore.

477
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:36,448
Right, Gavin?

478
00:18:36,532 --> 00:18:38,075
[suspicious music playing]

479
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:39,076
[titters]

480
00:18:39,785 --> 00:18:41,745
Okay. I thought you meant something else.

481
00:18:41,829 --> 00:18:42,371
No.

482
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:45,499
Chanty, you have
a lipstick stain here on--

483
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:47,334
- Rommel: There.
- Oh, oh.

484
00:18:47,417 --> 00:18:49,211
Excuse me, I'm just going to the restroom.

485
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:52,589
Goodness, bro.

486
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:55,342
You're really going to
break up with her now?

487
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:56,468
Right away?!

488
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:57,803
Bro, I don't want to
drag this out anymore.

489
00:18:57,886 --> 00:18:58,929
It's heading there anyway.

490
00:18:59,012 --> 00:19:01,306
That's the thing,
it's heading there anyway.

491
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,558
But it's your first date today, look,

492
00:19:02,641 --> 00:19:04,143
she's so happy.

493
00:19:04,685 --> 00:19:06,270
Don't hurt her yet.

494
00:19:07,104 --> 00:19:08,522
And let's first find a way

495
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:10,023
for us to be friends.

496
00:19:10,107 --> 00:19:11,191
Come on.

497
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:13,485
Rommel: Come on.

498
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:14,278
[music fades]

499
00:19:14,361 --> 00:19:14,903
[chuckles softly]

500
00:19:14,987 --> 00:19:16,280
You're right.

501
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,907
There are so many broken marriages now.

502
00:19:20,159 --> 00:19:21,994
There are so many flirts now.

503
00:19:22,870 --> 00:19:27,207
Or it could be that there
are so many spineless men now.

504
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:29,042
It's a two-way street.

505
00:19:29,126 --> 00:19:31,753
I'm sure Atoy is loyal to you.

506
00:19:31,837 --> 00:19:32,629
[rousing music playing]

507
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:34,506
What exactly is his work?

508
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:35,757
Why are you asking?

509
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,677
I'm just curious.

510
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:40,262
Do you drink?

511
00:19:40,345 --> 00:19:42,514
Maybe we can still catch happy hour.

512
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:44,850
I thought you were
on a solo staycation here?

513
00:19:44,933 --> 00:19:47,811
Well, I just want someone to talk to

514
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,354
over a few drinks.

515
00:19:49,438 --> 00:19:52,065
You know, get to know each other.

516
00:19:52,149 --> 00:19:53,650
Georgia: We can be friends.

517
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,195
My boss needs me.

518
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,823
It looks like that stain

519
00:19:59,907 --> 00:20:01,950
on your dress won't come out.

520
00:20:02,451 --> 00:20:03,994
There's a boutique where you can buy

521
00:20:04,077 --> 00:20:05,579
a nice dress.

522
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:08,123
[tense music playing]

523
00:20:08,207 --> 00:20:09,583
See you around.

524
00:20:14,004 --> 00:20:14,713
[music fades]

525
00:20:14,796 --> 00:20:16,423
[rousing music playing]

526
00:20:16,506 --> 00:20:17,549
Atoy, I think…

527
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,344
it won’t be
a problem if the two meet, right?

528
00:20:20,427 --> 00:20:22,346
Because you haven't done anything wrong.

529
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,389
Of course. There really isn't, buddy.

530
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:27,267
But just to avoid trouble, buddy.

531
00:20:27,351 --> 00:20:28,602
And of course I still need to finish

532
00:20:28,685 --> 00:20:29,561
this mission, you know.

533
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:30,562
- Well…
- Huh?

534
00:20:31,313 --> 00:20:32,314
It might be better, 'Toy,

535
00:20:32,397 --> 00:20:33,857
if you're the one to call Audrey,

536
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,192
tell her…

537
00:20:35,275 --> 00:20:36,318
to leave, to go home.

538
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,153
Right? Just make an excuse.

539
00:20:39,821 --> 00:20:41,073
Well, Miss Ci--

540
00:20:41,156 --> 00:20:42,407
[phone ringing] Buddy, I'll leave

541
00:20:42,491 --> 00:20:43,659
- Audrey to you, okay.
- Okay, okay.

542
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:44,701
- Mmm.
- Buddy.

543
00:20:44,785 --> 00:20:46,161
Hello, Miss Cita?

544
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:48,455
Atoy: Yes. Is the customer there already?

545
00:20:48,538 --> 00:20:50,666
[phone keys clicking]

546
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:53,460
[phone blips]

547
00:20:53,543 --> 00:20:56,630
[suspicious music playing]

548
00:20:57,297 --> 00:20:58,507
I'll take care of it.

549
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:02,427
[music swells]

550
00:21:04,179 --> 00:21:04,846
[music fades]

551
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:07,641
Solo staycation, your face.

552
00:21:12,646 --> 00:21:14,147
Audrey, Audrey.

553
00:21:14,231 --> 00:21:16,733
- Um, Ms. Dolly!
- Do you have mosquito repellant?

554
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,026
- Mosquito repellant?
- Um… Dolly: Yes, please.

555
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,362
Because I swear, there's a mosquito

556
00:21:20,445 --> 00:21:22,572
following me around
and I think they work in shifts.

557
00:21:22,656 --> 00:21:23,657
They don't want to die.

558
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:24,825
- Citronella spray.
- Thank you so much.

559
00:21:24,908 --> 00:21:28,203
[light music playing]

560
00:21:33,625 --> 00:21:35,002
You can keep it for now.

561
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:36,253
[sighs]

562
00:21:36,336 --> 00:21:37,087
Thank you.

563
00:21:37,170 --> 00:21:38,547
Here you go.

564
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:40,382
What is this for?

565
00:21:40,465 --> 00:21:42,467
I am giving you my villa here.

566
00:21:42,551 --> 00:21:43,760
Wait, wait!

567
00:21:43,844 --> 00:21:45,429
Before you say anything.

568
00:21:46,763 --> 00:21:49,266
I'm not staying here after my meeting.

569
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:50,934
So please, call your husband,

570
00:21:51,018 --> 00:21:53,353
have him come here and you two can use it.

571
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:56,606
This seems too much, Ms. Dolly.

572
00:21:56,690 --> 00:21:59,192
And I'm not prepared to stay overnight.

573
00:21:59,276 --> 00:22:02,779
Audrey, there's a boutique in the resort.

574
00:22:02,863 --> 00:22:04,698
Buy yourself a new outfit.

575
00:22:04,781 --> 00:22:06,908
Dolly: Come on, don't be shy.

576
00:22:07,701 --> 00:22:09,036
You deserve a day off.

577
00:22:09,578 --> 00:22:10,829
Say yes.

578
00:22:10,912 --> 00:22:12,414
Yes?

579
00:22:12,497 --> 00:22:13,832
[light music playing]

580
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:15,000
Both: Yes.

581
00:22:15,083 --> 00:22:15,792
- Good.
- Yes.

582
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,544
- Thank you, Ms. Dolly.
- You are welcome.

583
00:22:17,627 --> 00:22:20,339
Um, have you seen Oka?

584
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:21,131
Ah, Oscar.

585
00:22:21,214 --> 00:22:22,507
Oscar? No.

586
00:22:22,591 --> 00:22:23,383
Okay. I have to go.

587
00:22:23,467 --> 00:22:25,052
I have to be somewhere. Enjoy.

588
00:22:25,135 --> 00:22:26,678
Dolly: Bye, bye!

589
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,637
Bye!

590
00:22:29,598 --> 00:22:30,849
[phone blips]

591
00:22:30,932 --> 00:22:33,060
Oscar, where are you?

592
00:22:37,439 --> 00:22:40,400
[ominous music playing]

593
00:22:44,321 --> 00:22:44,946
Pool.

594
00:22:46,156 --> 00:22:48,450
Pool. It should be here.

595
00:22:48,533 --> 00:22:49,618
Okay, pool.

596
00:22:50,952 --> 00:22:51,495
Okay.

597
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:52,412
[music fades]

598
00:22:52,496 --> 00:22:53,330
Okay, Sir.

599
00:22:54,081 --> 00:22:54,998
Okay, thank you.

600
00:22:55,082 --> 00:22:57,584
[rousing music playing]

601
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:03,673
Atoy?

602
00:23:03,757 --> 00:23:09,179
[tense music playing]

603
00:23:09,721 --> 00:23:10,555
Audrey?

604
00:23:11,389 --> 00:23:15,227
[music swells]

605
00:23:17,729 --> 00:23:19,898
[electronic blipping]

606
00:23:21,358 --> 00:23:25,654
[intense music playing]

607
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,119
Who is Samir talking to?

608
00:23:32,702 --> 00:23:35,497
Then we need to be extra careful now!

609
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:38,875
That means The Washer is here.

610
00:23:38,959 --> 00:23:39,543
[thuds softly]

611
00:23:40,168 --> 00:23:41,503
Brother, really! You don’t--

612
00:23:41,586 --> 00:23:42,671
[speaks in Russian]

613
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,965
He speaks Russian?

614
00:23:45,048 --> 00:23:45,841
Hey!

615
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:47,926
Audrey, my dear!

616
00:23:48,009 --> 00:23:49,010
- Ms. Dolly!
- Hello.

617
00:23:49,094 --> 00:23:50,971
Good thing your husband made it.

618
00:23:51,054 --> 00:23:52,931
He didn't get lost in another house.

619
00:23:53,014 --> 00:23:54,432
I mean, in another resort.

620
00:23:54,516 --> 00:23:56,101
Ah, hello again, Ma'am.

621
00:23:56,184 --> 00:23:58,395
Thank you also for the overnight stay.

622
00:23:58,478 --> 00:23:59,980
Believe it or not,

623
00:24:00,063 --> 00:24:01,398
I already know who she is.

624
00:24:01,481 --> 00:24:03,483
She just looks like
a somewhat well-off mother,

625
00:24:03,567 --> 00:24:05,735
but I'm sure she's The Washer!

626
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:09,489
Atoy and his wife are in cahoots?

627
00:24:09,573 --> 00:24:10,782
That's why I don't believe

628
00:24:10,866 --> 00:24:12,659
they only came here for a vacation.

629
00:24:12,742 --> 00:24:14,119
Are we reporting now? Oh, okay, okay.

630
00:24:14,202 --> 00:24:15,203
Emerson: What are your updates?

631
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:16,997
Atoy, Samir is here.

632
00:24:17,080 --> 00:24:21,585
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
